  "goodToKnow": "Die Raststätte is a motorway service station with petrol, restaurant, shop and toilets, directly on the Autobahn. Most are run by one company, Tank & Rast, and toilets charge a fee with a voucher. A simpler Rastplatz (lay-by) may have only parking and toilets, while an Autohof just off the exit is often cheaper. Rasten means to rest on a journey: Wer rastet, der rostet (use it or lose it). Plural: die Raststätten."
